This is a 4-step verified retrosynthetic route. The strategy: (1) Horner–Wadsworth–Emmons olefination installs the terminal acrylic acid using dimethyl phosphonoacetic acid; (2) a second HWE installs the conjugated diene using dimethyl(2-oxoethyl)phosphonate; (3 & 4) custom templates (1914390/1914391) construct the central trisubstituted tetrahydropyran scaffold and its sidechains from the chiral THP-aldehyde building block and the Still–Gennari alkynyl phosphonate reagent. All steps were individually verified, and the route passes schema validation within the 5-step limit.
